Z||000000||TRiAD||11-09-2001||12:08 PM||||OK, so I buy this car, and it's tough to shift, I expected that. From what I was told, all the 4spds and Getrags were like that, and only the 5sp Isuzu shifts like the Hondas I'm used to. <BR>It got tougher and tougher to shift and find the gears, and I was sure something wasn't right...then...<P>"thunk!"..."DING dingdinggg  dindingggg..." Something metal and small went down the road beside me. <P>"Crap! It's broke!"<P>Well...now it's EASIER to shift?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Was there something unnecessary jammed in there?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85-Sig-2.gif">              <BR><B><I><u><FONT COLOR="red">TRiAD Motorsports</FONT></u></B> \\\\ <B>triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> //// Michael ~ 85 GT 4sp</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||11-09-2001||02:46 PM||||What fell out?  Did you go back and pick it up?<P>If it fell off, it certainly wasn't needed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jefrysuko||11-09-2001||03:14 PM||||I bet you broke the retaining clip that holds the cable in place on the trans.  Go have someone move the shifter around look to see if the cable is flopping around freely.  I have also heard that the the brackets that the shift cables are attached to tend to crack and this could cause similar problems.<P>The 4-speeds have a nylon bushing that is prone to wear and could make it hard to shift.  Rodney makes some replacement brass ones that work better than the nylon ones ever did.<P>Take a look and see if you can figure out what is broken and get back to us.  Then check out those bushings (they are on the pivot point of a stamped steel lever that pushes and pulls on the selector shaft if I remember right).||||reg||1
